        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The VIP is the contract",
          "text": "Clients bind to the ==VIP==, never to a backend IP, so servers can be replaced, drained or rebuilt freely. Everything later hangs on **connection vs request** (p2)."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==L4==: reads ==TCP/UDP headers only== — the __5-tuple__",
            "`src IP | src port | dst IP | dst port | proto`",
            "Payload **never** parsed — bytes are opaque",
            "==L7==: terminates the connection, parses the app protocol",
            "HTTP method/path/headers/cookies, gRPC service, TLS __SNI__"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "L4: SYN",
                "sub": "pick backend once"
              },
              {
                "text": "flow pinned",
                "sub": "5-tuple in table"
              },
              {
                "text": "all packets",
                "sub": "same backend, for life",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
