          "text": "4. What each buys you",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**L7**: `/api`→svc-A, `/static`→S3, header/cookie routing",
            "**L7**: retries, URL rewrites, response buffering, per-request metrics",
            "**L4**: protocol-blind — {green:Postgres}, {green:Redis}, {green:SMTP}, {green:QUIC} all work",
            "**L4**: µs overhead, __millions__ of concurrent conns per node"
          ],
          "style": "star"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "# L7 route table",
            "- path: /api/   -> svc-a:8080",
            "- path: /static -> svc-b:8080",
            "- header: x-canary=1 -> svc-a-v2",
            "# L4 sees only: tcp/443 -> pool"
          ],
          "note": "L4 cannot express any of these"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "L4 for ==scale and protocol independence==; L7 for ==routing and per-request fairness==. Put L4 in front, L7 behind — never one L7 hop doing both."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# on each BACKEND, not the LB",
            "ip addr add 10.0.0.5/32 dev lo",
            "sysctl -w \\",
            "  net.ipv4.conf.all.arp_ignore=1",
            "  net.ipv4.conf.all.arp_announce=2"
          ],
          "note": "missing suppression = VIP ARP war"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Tunnel: LB encapsulates, backend decaps — **any L2 segment**",
            "IPIP costs 20B of header, GRE 24B",
            "Clamp MSS to ~1400 or big replies blackhole on PMTUD"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
