      "page_title": "Inside an L4 Balancer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The real design",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "chain",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Two-tier edge",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "L4 edge (NLB / ECMP)",
                "note": "raw pps, SYN-flood + DDoS absorb, TLS passthrough",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "L7 tier (Envoy / NGINX)",
                "note": "terminates TLS, routes per request, retries",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "Backend pool",
                "note": "HTTP/1.1 or gRPC, balanced evenly",
                "ink": "black"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Three Forwarding Modes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "LB rewrites",
            "Return path",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{green:NAT}",
              "dst IP in, src out",
              "back through LB",
              "2x LB bandwidth"
            ],
            [
              "{blue:DSR}",
              "dst **MAC** only",
              "direct to client",
              "LB blind to reply"
            ],
            [
              "{purple:Tunnel}",
              "IPIP / GRE wrap",
              "direct to client",
              "eats ==MTU=="
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. NAT Mode",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "In: LB rewrites ==dst IP== VIP `10.0.0.5` to backend `10.1.1.7`",
            "Out: LB rewrites ==src IP== back to the VIP",
            "Return traffic **must** transit the LB (default gw or SNAT)",
            "Payoff: LB sees both directions — real counts, retries, 5xx",
            "Price: every response byte crosses the LB again"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. DSR and Tunnel Mode",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "LB swaps only the **dst MAC**; IP headers untouched",
            "Backend answers the client directly — ==asymmetric path==",
            "Backend must own the VIP on `lo`, __ARP suppressed__",
            "LB cannot see or count responses: ingress stats only",
            "Egress win is huge for video / CDN (10:1 out vs in)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. In the Wild",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "ipvsadm -A -t 10.0.0.5:80 -s wlc",
            "ipvsadm -a -t 10.0.0.5:80 \\",
            "  -r 10.1.1.7:80 -g",
            "# -g DSR  -m NAT  -i tunnel",
            "ipvsadm -lnc   # the flow table"
          ],
          "note": "-g needs the VIP on backend lo"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "L4 rule of thumb",
          "text": "State buys accuracy, hashing buys ==scale==. NAT to see the traffic, DSR or tunnel to move it cheaply, Maglev so a **deploy** does not reset every live connection."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "linux",
      "subtitle": "NAT, DSR, flow hashing"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Flow State, Maglev and Kernel Datapaths",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Flow Table vs Stateless Hash",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "Flow table",
            "Stateless hash"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "State",
              "5-tuple → backend",
              "none"
            ],
            [
              "Max conns",
              "**table size**",
              "unbounded"
            ],
            [
              "Mid-flow",
              "pinned entry",
              "stable hash only"
            ],
            [
              "Scale-out",
              "state per node",
              "**ECMP** fan-out"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Rehash, Maglev, Draining",
          "items": [
            "`hash % N`: change N and ==~all flows== remap — every conn resets",
            "Maglev: fixed table (65537 slots), weighted permutations fill it",
            "Membership change disturbs only ~1/N of slots, spread stays even",
            "Drain at L4: hash no **new** flows, keep old entries till FIN or timeout"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{icon:linux} **IPVS**: in-kernel L4, netfilter path, ~hundreds of kpps",
            "**Katran** / {icon:kubernetes} **Cilium**: XDP+eBPF in the NIC driver path",
            "XDP skips skb alloc and conntrack — millions of pps per box"
          ],
          "style": "star"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "NAT with a backend route that skips the LB — asymmetric **drop**",
            "DSR backend replying to ARP for the VIP — it steals the VIP",
            "Reading DSR byte counters: the LB only ever saw ingress",
            "Tunnel with no MSS clamp — small requests fine, big replies hang",
            "Modulo hashing on an autoscaling pool: every deploy kills all flows"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What L7 Proxying Is",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "L7 LB __terminates__ the client connection, parses ==HTTP==, and re-issues each request onto a **separate** backend connection. Two independent connection lifetimes, not one wire.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Request Lifecycle",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "accept",
                "sub": "TCP"
              },
              {
                "text": "TLS",
                "sub": "handshake"
              },
              {
                "text": "parse",
                "sub": "line+hdrs"
              },
              {
                "text": "route",
                "sub": "match"
              },
              {
                "text": "pick",
                "sub": "backend"
              },
              {
                "text": "stream",
                "sub": "resp+log"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Buffering vs Streaming",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Wins",
            "Costs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Full buffer",
              "slowloris absorbed",
              "+latency, RAM/disk"
            ],
            [
              "Streaming",
              "TTFB low, uploads cheap",
              "slow client pins a worker"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "nginx",
      "subtitle": "Proxying HTTP properly"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Connection Pools, Headers & Proxy Config",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Two Connection Pools",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Downstream==: one keepalive socket per client, idle-heavy",
            "==Upstream==: small pool, **reused** across many clients",
            "10k clients can share ~200 backend connections",
            "Pools scale independently — that is the whole point"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Protocol Adapter",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Client speaks",
            "LB does",
            "Backend gets"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "HTTP/2",
              "demux streams",
              "HTTP/1.1 pipeline"
            ],
            [
              "HTTP/3 QUIC",
              "de-QUIC",
              "HTTP/1.1"
            ],
            [
              "h2 + TLS1.3",
              "terminate, re-encrypt",
              "h2c cleartext"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Client identity headers",
          "items": [
            "`X-Forwarded-For: 203.0.113.9, 10.0.0.4` — append, never trust the last hop",
            "`X-Forwarded-Proto: https` — backend builds correct redirects",
            "`Forwarded: for=..;proto=..` — RFC 7239, one header",
            "==PROXY protocol== v2: same identity for **L4** hops, prepended before TLS bytes"
          ],
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Config Sketch",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "nginx",
          "lines": [
            "upstream api {",
            "  least_conn;",
            "  server 10.0.1.7:8080 max_fails=3;",
            "  keepalive 64;   # upstream pool",
            "}",
            "location /api/ {",
            "  proxy_connect_timeout 2s;",
            "  proxy_read_timeout   15s;",
            "  proxy_pass http://api;",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "keepalive needs HTTP/1.1 + empty Connection"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Cost stamp",
          "text": "TLS + header parse puts L7 at roughly ==10x L4 CPU== per unit of work — L4 counts packets, L7 counts requests. Buy routing, retries and per-request balance with that CPU, or stay at L4."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The __scheduler__ answers one question per arrival: ==which backend==. Everything else — health, affinity, failover — only edits the candidate set it picks from.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "txt",
          "lines": [
            "RR   : n0 n1 n2 n0 n1 n2",
            "WRR  : w=[3,1,1] naive",
            "       n0 n0 n0 n1 n2  # bunched",
            "smooth: n0 n1 n0 n2 n0  # spread"
          ],
          "note": "weights are integers, not ratios"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "nginx",
      "subtitle": "Proxying HTTP properly"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Timeouts, Retries and Round Robin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Timeout Ladder",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Timeout",
            "Typical",
            "Stops"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "connect",
              "1-2s",
              "dead/full backend"
            ],
            [
              "tls handshake",
              "5s",
              "stalled ClientHello"
            ],
            [
              "request header",
              "10s",
              "slowloris"
            ],
            [
              "idle keepalive",
              "60s",
              "socket leak"
            ],
            [
              "backend response",
              "15-30s",
              "hung app thread"
            ],
            [
              "total request",
              "60s",
              "infinite streaming"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Retries + Outliers",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Retry on **connect failure** or `GET/HEAD/PUT` only — never blind `POST`",
            "==Retry budget== 20%: retries capped as share of live traffic",
            "Eject after **5** consecutive 5xx; base eject 30s, ×N per ejection",
            "Cap ejection at 50% of pool, re-admit slowly — passive, not the health check"
          ],
          "style": "number"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Trusting `X-Forwarded-For` verbatim — client can forge it",
            "Retrying non-idempotent POST, double-charging a card",
            "No retry budget: one blip becomes a **stampede**",
            "Streaming mode with no header timeout = slowloris open door"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism: the stateless pair",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Round robin==: cycle in order. `O(1)`, **zero** state",
            "Correct only if nodes and requests are homogeneous",
            "==Random==: `O(1)`, no state, fine at big pool sizes",
            "Random's cost: a **fat tail** — unlucky nodes stack up"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Mechanism: load-aware",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Least connections==: fewest active conns wins. Safest **default**",
            "Adapts to varying request duration, unlike RR",
            "==Weighted LC==: score = `active / weight`; 2x box takes 2x load",
            "==Least response time==: conns **+** an `EWMA` of latency"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. P2C and hashing",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "sample 2 at random",
                "sub": "no global view"
              },
              {
                "text": "compare load",
                "sub": "conns or EWMA"
              },
              {
                "text": "send to lighter",
                "sub": "O(1), near-LC quality"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "slow_start:",
            "  window: 30s   # 0 -> full",
            "  # weight ramps linearly"
          ],
          "note": "warm-up beats the empty-node dogpile"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "nginx",
      "subtitle": "Picking the Backend"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "P2C, Consistent Hashing and Herd Effects",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "txt",
          "lines": [
            "wlc:  a=[10,10] w=[1,2]",
            "      10/1=10 vs 10/2=5",
            "      -> pick n1",
            "lrt:  score = active * ewma_ms"
          ],
          "note": "EWMA sees a slow node before conns pile"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==P2C== needs **no** global state — ideal for distributed / mesh LBs",
            "==Hash== (src IP, URL, header): deterministic, for affinity + cache locality",
            "Hash is for **stickiness**, never for evenness",
            "==Bounded-load consistent hash==: cap a node at `(1+ε)×mean`, overflow spills on"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Comparison"
