  "caption": {
    "text": "Your load balancer is not a magic box that makes traffic disappear — it is a forwarding decision made thousands of times a second, and every layer of that decision has a failure mode. This handbook walks L4 versus L7, the scheduling algorithms that pick a backend, health checks that lie to you, sticky sessions that break scaling, and the failover paths that only get tested during an outage. Ten pages of handwritten notes on the mechanics and the trade-offs behind each.",
